.TH CLOCKIFY-LAUNCHERS 1 "July 2026" "clockify-launchers 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clockify-launchers \- create Ubuntu launchers that start Clockify timers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clockify-launchers
.RI [ command ] " " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates and maintains per-user application launchers that start Clockify
timers. Launchers appear in the GNOME application grid; clicking one starts
or switches the current timer. The Clockify API key is stored only in the
system keyring.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Open or focus the application window (default).
.TP
.BI "start --launcher " UUID
Start or switch the timer for one launcher.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the current user's running timer.
.TP
.BR sync " [" --background ]
Reconcile launchers with Clockify now. With \fB--background\fR, run quietly
for the systemd user timer.
.TP
.BR doctor " [" --network ]
Diagnose configuration and integration. Read-only by default.
.TP
.BR reset " [" --remove-launchers "] [" --yes ]
Reset application data. Previews what will be removed and touches only
application-owned files.
.TP
.BI "demo --state " STATE
Open the UI in a deterministic demo state.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success or a defined no-op. Nonzero codes: 2 configuration, 3
authentication, 4 API, 5 target, 6 desktop file, 7 partial switch, 8 locked.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clockify-launchers/config.json
Nonsecret configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/clockify-launchers/state.db
Local state database.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/applications/com.dribia.ClockifyLaunchers.*.desktop
Generated launchers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://docs.clockify.me/
Clockify API documentation
.UE
